      "page_title": "Delivery Semantics: The Three Guarantees",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Guarantees",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Semantic",
            "Loss",
            "Duplicates"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "possible",
              "impossible"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "impossible",
              "possible"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "none",
              "no dup effect"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "at-most-once: delivered zero or one time",
            "at-least-once: delivered one or more times",
            "exactly-once: exactly one observable effect"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Pipeline Property"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Spans produce + store + consume + side effects",
            "No single config flag grants it",
            "Two halves: producer-to-broker, consumer commit",
            "Each half is chosen independently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "produce",
              "store",
              "consume",
              "side effect"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The pipeline guarantee is the weakest of its links. An at-least-once producer plus an at-most-once consumer is at-most-once end to end."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Dupes And Loss Are Born"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Duplicates: retry after an ambiguous outcome",
            "Write committed, ack lost on the wire",
            "Loss: acking before the data is durable",
            "Loss: committing progress before processing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Retry Dilemma",
          "text": "On timeout you retry and risk a duplicate, or you don't and risk loss. Only deduplication escapes both."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Kafka Actually Dodges"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "EOS = exactly-once processing inside Kafka",
            "Not exactly-once delivery over a network",
            "Two-generals limit dodged with idempotence",
            "Ordering is a separate axis from count"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Pick By Workload",
          "items": [
            "Metrics, logs, traces: at-most-once is fine",
            "Billing, ledgers: exactly-once or idempotent sink",
            "Everything else: at-least-once, dedup at the sink"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Semantic",
            "Mechanism",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "fire-and-forget",
              "cheapest"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "ack + retry",
              "modest"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "retry + dedup",
              "coordination"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The acks Knob",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "acks",
            "Waits for",
            "Failure mode"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`0`",
              "nothing",
              "silent loss"
            ],
            [
              "`1`",
              "leader log write",
              "loss if leader dies"
            ],
            [
              "`all` / `-1`",
              "all in-sync replicas",
              "stall, not loss"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`acks=0` never waits for a broker response",
            "`acks=1` replies before followers replicate",
            "`acks=all` is required for any at-least or exactly claim"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Durability Needs Two Settings"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`min.insync.replicas` is a broker/topic setting",
            "`acks=all` with `min.insync.replicas=1` still loses",
            "Standard: RF=3, `min.insync.replicas=2`, `acks=all`",
            "Tolerates one broker loss without loss or stall"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Delivery Semantics: The Three Guarantees (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "var tp = new TopicPartition(t, p);",
            "var off = new OffsetAndMetadata(",
