        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`read_uncommitted` is the default, always",
            "It shows records the instant they are written",
            "Even ones a later abort throws away",
            "Without `read_committed` the machinery buys nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Last Stable Offset"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "LSO = offset of the earliest still-open transaction",
            "A `read_committed` consumer never reads past it",
            "One long transaction blocks that partition",
            "Committed records queued behind it wait too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "memory-cells",
          "spec": {
            "label": "log, LSO stuck at 102",
            "cells": [
              "100 done",
              "101 done",
              "102 open",
              "103 open",
              "104 open"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Client-Side Filtering"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Broker ships an aborted-transaction index per fetch",
            "The client drops aborted batches before your code",
            "Control markers never surface as records"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Offsets Are Not Contiguous",
          "text": "Never assume `offset + 1` is the next record. `consumer.position()` can exceed the last returned offset because of markers and filtered batches."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Latency And Design"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Records become visible only at commit time",
            "End-to-end latency includes transaction duration",
            "Keep transactions short",
            "Batch size trades throughput for visibility lag"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Stuck Transaction Symptom",
          "items": [
            "Consumer lag grows with no progress",
            "LSO frozen behind one open transaction",
            "`transaction.timeout.ms` eventually forces an abort"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Transactions: Atomic Multi-Partition Writes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Does `read_committed` remove duplicates?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "No — it only hides aborted data",
            "Application-level duplicates still get through",
            "Dedup is the producer's or the sink's job"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choice",
            "Win",
            "Loss"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`read_uncommitted`",
              "lowest latency",
              "dirty reads"
            ],
            [
              "`read_committed`",
              "clean data",
              "LSO-bounded lag"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Legs Of The Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Idempotent producer",
            "Transactional writes",
            "`read_committed` consumer",
            "No auto-commit anywhere"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "properties",
          "lines": [
