        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One transactional producer per consumer instance",
            "A shared `transactional.id` means mutual fencing",
            "`group.instance.id` cuts rebalance churn",
            "Fewer rebalances, fewer aborted transactions"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Streams Does It Cheaper"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`exactly_once_v2` uses one producer per instance",
            "The old `exactly_once` used one per partition",
            "Requires brokers 2.5+",
            "`exactly_once` and `_beta` names are gone in 4.0",
            "State stores write changelog in the same transaction"
