        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Latency Floor",
          "text": "For a `read_committed` consumer the floor is the transaction duration — nothing is visible before commit. Streams defaults near a 100ms commit interval for exactly this balance."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Levers That Matter More"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`linger.ms` and `batch.size` beat any EOS knob",
            "Batching amortizes everything downstream",
            "`compression.type=lz4` or `zstd` cuts network and disk",
            "Compression is per batch: bigger batches compress better"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Broker-Side Bill"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Memory grows with live PIDs and open transactions",
            "Many short-lived producers is an anti-pattern",
            "`__transaction_state` and `__consumer_offsets` are real topics",
            "Real writes, real replication, real disk",
            "Rebalances cost more: open transactions abort and replay"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pick By Number"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Semantic",
            "Throughput",
            "Safety"
